│ patch_description        │ Redesigned the ansatz block to reduce parameter count while keeping strong expressivity   │
│                          │ and better regularization via symmetry/parameter sharing. The new block:                  │
│                          │ - Uses pairwise parameter sharing for all single-qubit Euler rotations (qubits (0,1),     │
│                          │ (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) share the same parameters).                                           │
│                          │ - Employs a structured, dense entangling pattern: a full ring of CZ gates plus an         │
│                          │ additional set of “skip” CZ chords.                                                       │
│                          │ - Adds a small number of parameterized CRZ gates restricted to the same qubit pairs       │
│                          │ (again with shared parameters per pair).                                                  │
│                          │ This cuts circuit parameters from 24 per block to 16 per block (→ fewer total trainable   │
│                          │ parameters), which typically improves parameter efficiency and reduces train-test gap     │
│                          │ while preserving accuracy.                                                                │
│                          │ Only ANSATZ_SPEC inside EVOLVE-BLOCK is changed; all inputs/outputs and the fixed         │
│                          │ training/feature-map/re-uploading/measurement pipeline remain identical.                  │
