│ patch_description        │ This ansatz improves on the previous designs by implementing a mixed rotation axis        │
│                          │ strategy. Instead of using only RY gates in the input layer, I alternate between RY and   │
│                          │ RZ rotations on different qubits. This diversifies the input-axis pool while maintaining  │
│                          │ the same parameter count (16 per block). The alternating approach allows the circuit to   │
│                          │ explore feature correlations along different rotational axes, potentially capturing more  │
│                          │ complex patterns in the data. The entanglement structure uses two layers of CZ gates in a │
│                          │ ring topology for better qubit connectivity. I've also added a final RZ layer for output  │
│                          │ shaping. This design maintains a good balance between parameter efficiency (16 parameters │
│                          │ per block) and expressivity while reducing the gate count compared to the previous        │
│                          │ version, which should lead to faster training convergence.                                │
